   $q$Which sentence about Yusuf and his uncle has NO modifier error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Yusuf set up the telescope on the roof that his uncle had lent him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-misplaced-clause"},{"text":"Hoping to see the eclipse, the roof was where Yusuf set up his telescope.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-dangling-modifier"},{"text":"Yusuf almost waited three hours for the eclipse to begin.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-limiting-modifier"},{"text":"Hoping to see the eclipse, Yusuf climbed to the roof with his telescope.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Hoping to see the eclipse, Yusuf climbed to the roof with his telescope.$q$, $q$Only the correct choice puts "Yusuf," the one hoping, right after the opening phrase. The "lent him" sentence makes it sound like his uncle lent him the roof, and "almost waited" means he nearly waited but did not.$q$, 'draft', null)
