   $q$Chiara found a letter in Grandma Rosa's attic, and the letter was written in Italian. Which sentence says this clearly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Chiara found a letter in Grandma Rosa's attic written in Italian.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-next-to-wrong-noun"},{"text":"Chiara, written in Italian, found a letter in Grandma Rosa's attic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-attached-to-person"},{"text":"Written in Italian, Chiara found a letter in Grandma Rosa's attic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opening-phrase-wrong-subject"},{"text":"In Grandma Rosa's attic, Chiara found a letter written in Italian.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In Grandma Rosa's attic, Chiara found a letter written in Italian.$q$, $q$"Written in Italian" must sit right after "letter," and moving the attic phrase to the front makes room for that. In "Chiara found a letter in Grandma Rosa's attic written in Italian," the phrase follows "attic," so the attic seems to be written in Italian.$q$, 'draft', null)
